static const char _zs260_d[] = "no main\n\nThe unit being compiled declares no `main: function is { ... }`, so the compiler has no entry point to start from. Compilation is demand-driven: `main` is the root, and what it reaches is what gets checked and emitted. A unit with no `main` is a library -- compile the program that opens it instead, or add a `main`. `--eager` resolves every definition rather than what a root reaches, so it does not require one.";
